# Trained models and tokenised data. Regenerated by llm/<unit>_prepare_mmap.py and
# llm/<unit>_train.py; see reproduce.md. 29G and 481M respectively, so never committed.
llm/checkpoints/
llm/data/

# Training and sweep logs
llm/logs/
ngram/logs/
logs/

# Weights & Biases run directories
wandb/
llm/wandb/
qwen/wandb/

# LibriSpeech forced alignments: a symlink to data downloaded outside the project
data/librispeech-alignments

# PDFs built from design.md and results.md by hand. Drop these two lines if the built
# PDFs should travel with the sources
design.pdf
results.pdf
reproduce.pdf
paper.pdf

# Everything under docs/: the figures, the reference material carried over from the
# predecessor project, and the superseded material kept because this is not a git
# repository. None of it is needed to reproduce a result, and docs/assets/ is someone
# else's output rather than this project's source
docs/

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.ipynb_checkpoints/
*.egg-info/
.venv/
venv/

# Local Claude Code settings, as opposed to a shared .claude/settings.json
.claude/settings.local.json

# Dropbox leaves these behind when the project syncs from two machines at once
*conflicted copy*

# Editor and OS cruft
.DS_Store
*.swp
*~

# Deliberately NOT ignored, despite being generated: llm/per_utterance/ and
# ngram/per_utterance/ (11M and 1.6M of JSON). They are the only inputs
# utils/bootstrap.py needs, and regenerating them means rescoring every checkpoint or
# refitting every sweep, so they are the cheapest artefact that keeps the confidence
# intervals and seed-variance results reproducible without the 29G above. The sweep
# reports (ngram/*.md, llm/eval_bitrate.md, qwen/eval_bitrate.md) are tracked for the
# same reason.

# Claude Code's project instructions: working notes for the agent rather than project
# source, and they churn as the experiments move
CLAUDE.md
